  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Syracuse University is a distinguished private research institution located in Syracuse, New York. Since its founding in 1870, the university has grown into a major academic hub, offering over 200 majors and 100 minors across 13 academic units. It is well-regarded for its academic offerings, research opportunities, and vibrant campus atmosphere.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>At Syracuse University, you will join a diverse, global community with approximately 4,000 international students from over 100 countries. The campus offers a rich array of student experiences, including a variety of clubs, societies, and gaming and esports facilities. Whether you are interested in sports, technology, or cultural activities, there are numerous ways to get involved and make the most of your time on campus.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<ol><li><strong>Library</strong> The university offers extensive physical and digital resources to support your research and academic needs throughout your degree.</li><li><strong>Sports</strong> Syracuse University is home to the JMA Wireless Dome, a massive on-campus sport facility. Additionally, students have access to the Barnes Center at the Arch, which serves as a hub for health, wellness, and fitness, including a state-of-the-art gaming and esports centre.</li><li><strong>Laboratories</strong> The university maintains world-class research laboratories, including specialised spaces like the Milton Conrad Sport Technology Lab and the Nutrition Assessment, Consultation and Education (ACE) Center, providing you with hands-on, industry-relevant experience.</li><li><strong>Cafeteria</strong> You will find various dining options across campus, including the Susan R. Klenk Learning Café and Kitchens, which offers modern food laboratories alongside dining services.</li></ol><p>If you’re looking for budget-friendly accommodation options outside the campus, feel free to <a href=\"https://onelink.to/jb48ev\">download our app</a> and check out the <a href=\"https://edvoy.com/student/stays\">Stays</a> feature!</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Campuses",
      "value": "<p>&nbsp;</p><ul><li><strong>Main Campus:</strong> Located in Syracuse, New York, this campus serves as the primary hub for most academic, administrative, and student life facilities.</li><li><strong>South Campus:</strong> Home to additional student facilities, including the Goldstein Student Center and the Tennity Ice Pavilion.</li><li><strong>Other Locations:</strong> The university maintains a significant presence in cities such as New York City, Washington, D.C., and Los Angeles, providing students with unique opportunities for industry engagement and immersion programs. Additionally, Syracuse Abroad offers learning centres in locations like London, Florence, Madrid, Santiago, and Strasbourg.</li></ul>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
